time=2026-10-20T01:21:35.119Z level=INFO msg="model prompt" record=prov-2026-44a07768 attempt=1 prompt="## The change\n\nThe provenance create command, in two files.\n\nWiring, cmd/provenance/create_cmd.go (cobra package): a top-level command,\nuse \"create\", short \"Create a new provenance record (defaults to draft\nstatus)\", arity none. Flags, none with a default:\n- title (string): \"Pre-populate the title field\"\n- intent (string): \"Pre-populate the intent field\"\n- type (string): \"Set the tier type of the record (brief|blueprint|imprint)\"\n- tag (strings): \"Pre-populate tags (comma-separated; repeatable)\"\n- scope (strings): \"Pre-populate affected_scope (repeatable)\"\n- implements (string): \"Parent record id, or its at-uri (at://<did>/dev.provisio.provenance.record/<id>); pins implements_version to a local parent's current version\"\n- locked (bool): \"Create the record as a locked layer\"\n- no-edit (bool): \"Write without opening editor\"\n- id-suffix (string), short form i: \"Append service suffix to ID (e.g., user-service)\"\nOnly id-suffix has a short form.\n\nLogic, cmd/provenance/create_run.go (go package, package main). Imports,\neach its own addImport, exactly these: crypto/rand, encoding/hex, fmt, io, os,\nos/exec, path/filepath, strings, time, github.com/spf13/cobra,\ngithub.com/livecodelife/provenance/record. Functions:\n- func newID(year int, suffix string, taken map[string]bool) (string,\n  error): \"prov-<year>-<8 lowercase hex digits from crypto/rand>\", plus\n  \"-\"+suffix when suffix is not empty; retry up to 100 times while the id\n  is in taken, then return an error.\n- func runCreate(out io.Writer, cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error:\n  1. r, err := openRepo(cmd); return err on error. Read every flag with\n     cmd.Flags().GetString / GetStringArray / GetBool.\n  2. If type is not empty and record.Type(type).Valid(2) is false, return\n     fmt.Errorf(\"invalid type %q (brief|blueprint|imprint)\", type).\n  3. Tags: split every --tag value on commas, trim spaces, drop empty\n     pieces, keep order.\n  4. taken: every id from r.Store.List(), plus the Aliases of each record\n     loaded with r.Store.Load(id) (skip records that fail to load).\n     id, err := newID(time.Now().Year(), suffix, taken).\n  5. Declare `var implementsID, implementsURI string` and `var implementsVersion int`. If implements starts with \"at://\" (strings.HasPrefix),\n     the parent lives in another account: `id, ok := record.ParseImplementsURI(implements)`; when !ok return\n     fmt.Errorf(\"invalid --implements %q: want a record id or at://<did>/dev.provisio.provenance.record/<id>\", implements);\n     otherwise set implementsID = id, implementsURI = implements, leave implementsVersion at 0, and remember a\n     hint to print in step 9. Otherwise, if implements is not empty: parent, _, err := r.resolve(implements);\n     return err on error; pin to parent.ID and parent.Version.\n  6. Build rec := &record.Record{Schema: 2, ID: id, Title: title, Type:\n     record.Type(type), Status: record.StatusDraft, CreatedAt:\n     time.Now().Format(\"2006-01-02\"), Author: r.author(), Version: 1,\n     Intent: intent, Locked: locked, Implements, ImplementsURI and\n     ImplementsVersion from step 5}, with Constraints, AffectedScope (the --scope values),\n     ForbiddenScope, Related, AssociatedTraces, Monitors and Tags never nil\n     (use []string{} when empty) and AssociatedSpecs []record.AssociatedSpec{}.\n  7. r.Store.Save(rec, nil); return err on error. path :=\n     filepath.Join(r.Root, r.recordPath(id)).\n  8. Unless --no-edit: run $EDITOR (or \"vi\" when unset) with path as its\n     one argument, with os.Stdin, os.Stdout and os.Stderr attached; if it\n     fails, print \"Warning: Could not open editor: <err>\" to os.Stderr and\n     carry on.\n  9. Print \"\\n✓ Created <path>\\n\\n\" to out; then, only when step 5 took the at-uri\n     branch, print \"  The parent is in another account, so implements_version is 0 (unpinned); run provenance repin once the parent can be read.\\n\\n\" to out. No snapshot is\n     written: a draft is freely editable until open writes version 1.\n\nHelpers that already exist in package main (call them; do not redefine\nthem): func openRepo(cmd *cobra.Command) (*repo, error); type repo struct {\nRoot string; Store *record.FilesStore; ... }; func (r *repo) resolve(id\nstring) (*record.Record, *record.Document, error), which prints its own\nmessage; func (r *repo) recordPath(id string) string (relative to r.Root);\nfunc (r *repo) author() string. Record library: record.Record and\nrecord.AssociatedSpec as above, record.Type, (record.Type).Valid(schema\nint) bool, record.StatusDraft, (*record.FilesStore).List() ([]string,\nerror), .Load(id) (*record.Record, *record.Document, error), .Save(r\n*record.Record, doc *record.Document) error.\n\n## Constraints on it\n\n- Both files are grown by sedum-haiku (--only prov-2026-44a07768): wiring with cobra, logic with go. Nothing in them is hand-written; a wrong result is fixed by revising this record and regrowing.\n- cmd/provenance/create_test.go is the hand-written gate.\n\n## Supplementary context\n\nThis section is supplied by the caller, not by the record. It is advisory: it does not add to or change what the record authorized, and the files below remain the only ones the actions may reach.\n\nSelections made for this change on an earlier run (context only; they are not applied):\n\n- {\"action\":\"setArgs\",\"kwargs\":{\"arity\":\"none\",\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"create\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addFlag\",\"kwargs\":{\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"create\",\"flag\":\"title\",\"type\":\"string\",\"usage\":\"Pre-populate the title field\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addFlag\",\"kwargs\":{\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"create\",\"flag\":\"intent\",\"type\":\"string\",\"usage\":\"Pre-populate the intent field\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addFlag\",\"kwargs\":{\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"create\",\"flag\":\"type\",\"type\":\"string\",\"usage\":\"Set the tier type of the record (brief|blueprint|imprint)\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addFlag\",\"kwargs\":{\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"create\",\"flag\":\"tag\",\"type\":\"strings\",\"usage\":\"Pre-populate tags (comma-separated; repeatable)\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addFlag\",\"kwargs\":{\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"create\",\"flag\":\"scope\",\"type\":\"strings\",\"usage\":\"Pre-populate affected_scope (repeatable)\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addFlag\",\"kwargs\":{\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"create\",\"flag\":\"implements\",\"type\":\"string\",\"usage\":\"Parent record id; pins implements_version to its current version\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addFlag\",\"kwargs\":{\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"create\",\"flag\":\"locked\",\"type\":\"bool\",\"usage\":\"Create the record as a locked layer\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addFlag\",\"kwargs\":{\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"create\",\"flag\":\"no-edit\",\"type\":\"bool\",\"usage\":\"Write without opening editor\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addShortFlag\",\"kwargs\":{\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"create\",\"flag\":\"id-suffix\",\"shorthand\":\"i\",\"type\":\"string\",\"usage\":\"Append service suffix to ID (e.g., user-service)\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/create_run.go\",\"path\":\"crypto/rand\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/create_run.go\",\"path\":\"fmt\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/create_run.go\",\"path\":\"os\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/create_run.go\",\"path\":\"os/exec\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/create_run.go\",\"path\":\"path/filepath\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/create_run.go\",\"path\":\"strings\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/create_run.go\",\"path\":\"time\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/create_run.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/spf13/cobra\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/create_run.go\",\"path\":\"encoding/hex\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/create_run.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/create_run.go\",\"path\":\"io\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func newID(year int, suffix string, taken map[string]bool) (string, error) {\\n\\tfor i := 0; i \\u003c 100; i++ {\\n\\t\\tb := make([]byte, 4)\\n\\t\\tif _, err := rand.Read(b); err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tid := fmt.Sprintf(\\\"prov-%d-%s\\\", year, hex.EncodeToString(b))\\n\\t\\tif suffix != \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\t\\tid += \\\"-\\\" + suffix\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif !taken[id] {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn id, nil\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn \\\"\\\", fmt.Errorf(\\\"could not generate a unique id after 100 attempts\\\")\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/create_run.go\",\"name\":\"newID\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func runCreate(out io.Writer, cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {\\n\\tr, err := openRepo(cmd)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\ttitle, _ := cmd.Flags().GetString(\\\"title\\\")\\n\\tintent, _ := cmd.Flags().GetString(\\\"intent\\\")\\n\\ttyp, _ := cmd.Flags().GetString(\\\"type\\\")\\n\\ttags, _ := cmd.Flags().GetStringArray(\\\"tag\\\")\\n\\tscope, _ := cmd.Flags().GetStringArray(\\\"scope\\\")\\n\\timplements, _ := cmd.Flags().GetString(\\\"implements\\\")\\n\\tlocked, _ := cmd.Flags().GetBool(\\\"locked\\\")\\n\\tnoEdit, _ := cmd.Flags().GetBool(\\\"no-edit\\\")\\n\\tsuffix, _ := cmd.Flags().GetString(\\\"id-suffix\\\")\\n\\n\\tif typ != \\\"\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 !record.Type(typ).Valid(2) {\\n\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"invalid type %q (brief|blueprint|imprint)\\\", typ)\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tcleanTags := []string{}\\n\\tfor _, t := range tags {\\n\\t\\tfor _, p := range strings.Split(t, \\\",\\\") {\\n\\t\\t\\tp = strings.TrimSpace(p)\\n\\t\\t\\tif p != \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcleanTags = append(cleanTags, p)\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\ttaken := map[string]bool{}\\n\\tids, err := r.Store.List()\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tfor _, existing := range ids {\\n\\t\\ttaken[existing] = true\\n\\t\\tloaded, _, err := r.Store.Load(existing)\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tfor _, a := range loaded.Aliases {\\n\\t\\t\\ttaken[a] = true\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tid, err := newID(time.Now().Year(), suffix, taken)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tvar implementsID string\\n\\tvar implementsVersion int\\n\\tif implements != \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\tparent, _, err := r.resolve(implements)\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\timplementsID = parent.ID\\n\\t\\timplementsVersion = parent.Version\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tif scope == nil {\\n\\t\\tscope = []string{}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\trec := \\u0026record.Record{\\n\\t\\tSchema:            2,\\n\\t\\tID:                id,\\n\\t\\tTitle:             title,\\n\\t\\tType:              record.Type(typ),\\n\\t\\tStatus:            record.StatusDraft,\\n\\t\\tCreatedAt:         time.Now().Format(\\\"2006-01-02\\\"),\\n\\t\\tAuthor:            r.author(),\\n\\t\\tVersion:           1,\\n\\t\\tIntent:            intent,\\n\\t\\tLocked:            locked,\\n\\t\\tImplements:        implementsID,\\n\\t\\tImplementsVersion: implementsVersion,\\n\\t\\tConstraints:       []string{},\\n\\t\\tAffectedScope:     scope,\\n\\t\\tForbiddenScope:    []string{},\\n\\t\\tRelated:           []string{},\\n\\t\\tAssociatedTraces:  []string{},\\n\\t\\tMonitors:          []string{},\\n\\t\\tTags:              cleanTags,\\n\\t\\tAssociatedSpecs:   []record.AssociatedSpec{},\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tif err := r.Store.Save(rec, nil); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tpath := filepath.Join(r.Root, r.recordPath(id))\\n\\n\\tif !noEdit {\\n\\t\\teditor := os.Getenv(\\\"EDITOR\\\")\\n\\t\\tif editor == \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\t\\teditor = \\\"vi\\\"\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tc := exec.Command(editor, path)\\n\\t\\tc.Stdin = os.Stdin\\n\\t\\tc.Stdout = os.Stdout\\n\\t\\tc.Stderr = os.Stderr\\n\\t\\tif err := c.Run(); err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \\\"Warning: Could not open editor: %v\\\\n\\\", err)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \\\"\\\\n✓ Created %s\\\\n\\\\n\\\", path)\\n\\treturn nil\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/create_run.go\",\"name\":\"runCreate\"}}\n\n## Already present\n\nThese regions already exist in the files below and belong to other changes. Do not select them: an action that resolves to one of them would conflict with the change that owns it.\n\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: describeRoot {\"bin\":\"provenance\"} (owned by prov-2026-76a125e6; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: addShortPersistentFlag:string {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"flag\":\"config\"} (owned by prov-2026-76a125e6; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"check\"} (owned by prov-2026-063f1395; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"status\"} (owned by prov-2026-12b1ca97; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"deprecate\"} (owned by prov-2026-35439261; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"complete\"} (owned by prov-2026-41fb548c; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"edit\"} (owned by prov-2026-57b8a95b; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"revise\"} (owned by prov-2026-5f69977b; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"